# Package layering

Dependencies flow **downward**. Lower layers never import apps.

```text
apps/web  --HTTP only-->  apps/api
apps/api / workers  -->  @repo/gcp-firebase
                         -->  @repo/firestore-converters
                              -->  @repo/shared-types / @repo/entities / …
```

See `docs/guides/firestore-collections.md`.

## Rules

| Allowed | Forbidden |
|---------|-----------|
| Apps import `@repo/*` | Packages import `apps/*` |
| Web → API over HTTP | Web reading/writing Firestore business docs |
| `@repo/gcp-firebase` for Admin Firestore | `firebase-admin/firestore` / `firebase/firestore` in apps (use adapters) |
| `@repo/ai-engine` public entrypoints | Apps importing `packages/ai-engine/src/clients/internal/**` |
| Web: `@repo/ai-context/storage` | Bare `@repo/ai-context` in web (Node `fs` risk) |

AI import matrix: `docs/ai-platform/01-architecture.md` (Import rules).

## Persistence

- Repository **interfaces** in `@repo/firestore-converters`
- Firestore **implementations** in `@repo/gcp-firebase`
- Wire in `apps/api/src/server.ts` and worker entrypoints

When adding a Firestore repository file under `packages/gcp-firebase/src/`, update the ESLint allowlist override that permits SDK usage in adapter files.

## Enforcement

- Package ESLint configs (`apps/api`, `firestore-converters`, `gcp-firebase`, `ai-engine`)
- `pnpm lint`, `pnpm lint:circular`
- Browser-safe AI import tests in web

